{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented on branch `impl-d52f`, commit `8c63584fd868ac763d9caca25fe992dabae5053a`.\n\n## AC evidence\n\n**AC1 — no `_heldout` path remains.** `git ls-files | grep -c '_heldout'` reads **0** on the post-change tree (it read 6 before). The expression filters *paths*, so the 57 `_heldout_` strings inside the tracked `.test_durations` and the occurrences in `src/rebar/reconciler/` and `docs/` are out of its scope by construction.\n\n**AC2 — five renames, per-module counts preserved exactly.** Measured by collecting each module before and after:\n\n| from | to | tests |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/interfaces/facades/test_attestation_parity_heldout_2e16.py` | `test_attestation_parity.py` | 8 |\n| `tests/unit/metrics/test_dead_values_heldout_7504.py` | `test_dead_values.py` | 4 |\n| `tests/unit/test_reviewed_tree_binding_heldout_da31.py` | `test_reviewed_tree_binding.py` | 9 |\n| `tests/unit/test_snapshot_contract_heldout_8537.py` | **`test_snapshot_schema_contract.py`** (deviation, below) | 9 |\n| `tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_update_priority_heldout_c9c6.py` | `test_update_priority.py` | 5 |\n\n**AC3 — the merge.** The 10 tests from `test_code_review_provenance_heldout_2d1c.py` now live in `tests/unit/test_code_review_provenance.py`, which goes from 3 tests to **13**. There were zero test-name collisions between the two modules, and zero helper-name collisions (`_git`/`_stub_gate_run`/`repo_with_origin`/`_DIFF` against `_enable`/`_verdict`/`PROVENANCE`). The source module is deleted. Two function-local `from rebar.llm.workflow import gate_dispatch` imports were dropped because the merge target already imports that symbol at module level; the merged tests now also inherit the target's `pytestmark = pytest.mark.unit`, which does not change their selection since they already sat under `tests/unit/`.\n\n**AC4 — whole-suite collection unchanged.** 20673 before, **20673** after. Exactly equal: no test was lost or silently duplicated.\n\n**AC5 — detection expression.** 6 on the pre-change tree, 0 after.\n\nTargeted run of all six affected modules: **61 passed**. `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, `mypy src/rebar scripts`, the complexity ratchet (`active=27 new=0 increased=0 stale=22`) and the mechanism ratchet all pass via the pre-commit hook.\n\n## Documented deviation from the plan\n\nThe plan named `tests/unit/test_snapshot_contract.py` as the rename target. That basename is **already taken** by `tests/integration/reconciler/jira_contract/test_snapshot_contract.py`. Neither `tests/unit/` nor `tests/integration/reconciler/jira_contract/` is a package — only 13 `tests/**/__init__.py` exist and neither directory has one — and `pyproject.toml` configures no pytest `importmode`, so collection runs in the default `prepend` mode. Under `prepend`, two same-basename modules in two non-package directories abort collection with an import-file-mismatch error. The plan's literal target would have broken the suite outright.\n\n`test_snapshot_schema_contract.py` is also the more accurate name: the module validates the snapshot JSON schema's accept/reject behaviour, which is a different subject from the integration contract test it would have collided with. Verified 0 remaining basename collisions across the tree after the rename.\n\n## Noted, not acted on\n\n`.test_durations` is tracked and holds 57 now-stale `_heldout_` test ids. Nothing polices its freshness — its only three references (`scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py:54`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_bridge_vocabulary_stale.py:32`, `tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py:171`) are all *exclusion*-list entries. Stale ids there degrade pytest-split's balancing slightly on the next split run and regenerate themselves; they fail nothing. Left alone as out of scope.\n\n`make verify` is queued behind the verify currently running in another worktree."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793653522897135659,"uuid":"f3a1448a-eefa-4200-ace7-34823e6bd8ae"}